# The stage box's settings. It lives on the SD card's boot partition as stage.conf, so any computer can
# edit it (the partition is FAT); the box reads it at every start. One KEY=value per line; a missing or
# empty value takes the default shown. Nothing secret goes here (the Wi-Fi is set when the card is imaged).

# ONE BOX PER ROBOT: it is named opendubs<N>-stage after its robot when the card is imaged (opendubs2-stage
# for opendubs2), and points at that robot here.
# The robot's stage page. The box tries ROBOT_URL first (the robot's mDNS name), then ROBOT_FALLBACK (its
# reserved address on the robot's network), and keeps trying both until one answers.
ROBOT_URL=http://opendubs2.local:8080/stage/
ROBOT_FALLBACK=http://10.42.2.10:8080/stage/

# The screen's mode. Empty: whatever the screen says it prefers (its EDID). Or force one, e.g.
# 1920x1080@60, for a screen that reports a mode it cannot really show. Changing it restarts the box once.
MODE=

# Where the show's music goes, until the dashboard's Stage box card sets it (that choice is kept on the
# media stick and wins): auto, hdmi, jack, usb or bt.
#   auto  the screen's speaker if it says it has one, else a USB audio adapter, else a paired Bluetooth
#         speaker that is connected, else the 3.5 mm jack (a Raspberry Pi 4 only: a Pi 5 has none)
AUDIO=auto

